{
  "fixture_version": 1,
  "description": "Built-in masking of opt-in text fields (prompt_text, response_text, action_details.feedback_text, intent_summary) and of span content. Each SDK's built-in masking must turn every input into its expected output exactly. `rules` lists the rules in application order: `pattern` is the exact regular expression source both SDKs compile (no flags; applied globally, left to right, without overlaps); every match is replaced by `tokens[token]` unless `check` names a validation the match must pass (luhn: Luhn checksum; ipv6: 8 groups, or fewer with one `::`; phone: 10-12 digits, 9-15 after a leading +; ssn: area not 000/666/900-999, group not 00, serial not 0000; iban: 15-34 alphanumerics without spaces and ISO 7064 mod-97 == 1); with `keep_group: 1` only the text after capture group 1 is replaced. Each rule runs over the previous rule's output, so the first rule to match a span wins. Text longer than 32000 code points is not masked: the field is withheld (`expected: null`). A case with `repeat: n` means input and expected are each repeated n times. Names and postal addresses are not caught.",
  "tokens": {
    "email": "[email]",
    "phone": "[phone]",
    "card": "[card]",
    "ip": "[ip]",
    "secret": "[secret]",
    "ssn": "[ssn]",
    "iban": "[iban]"
  },
